    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS). The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the per-city capacity rule: creating an owner is rejected with **409 Conflict** when that owner's city already contains 50 or more owners.\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor function-injection pattern (not Spring MVC), I added:\n\n1. **`CheckOwnerCityCapacity`** (`function/owner/`) \u2014 a pipeline step that reads the built `@Val Owner`, counts existing owners whose city matches case-insensitively (consistent with the existing customer-code logic), and throws when the count is \u2265 50. It runs after `BuildOwner`/household checks and before save, so only pre-existing owners are counted.\n\n2. **`CityAtCapacityException`** (`escalation/`) \u2014 a checked exception (`extends Exception`) so it surfaces in the `throws` clause.\n\n3. **`CityAtCapacityExceptionHandler`** (`escalation/`) \u2014 maps the exception to a 409 `ProblemDetail` response, mirroring the existing `DuplicateHousehold`/`DuplicateTelephone` handlers.\n\n4. **Escalation YAML** \u2014 `officefloor/escalation/\u2026CityAtCapacityException.yml` wiring the exception to its handler.\n\n5. **Wired the step** into `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` as `checkCityCapacity` between `checkHousehold` and `countNamesakes`, under `govern: [ transaction ]` like its neighbors.\n\nThe provided `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` (fills a city to 50, expects the 51st to be a 409) passes, and the full suite is green.",
